{"id":"0588da4f-ab9b-4f56-a88d-729db56dcd46","body":"Finding: production has `pg_stat_monitor` installed in `public`, but it isn't in `shared_preload_libraries`, so it has never collected anything. Nothing uses it. We'll drop it instead of moving it: a migration runs `DROP EXTENSION IF EXISTS pg_stat_monitor;`, and its line comes out of `extensions.sql`. The goal is unchanged: the Security Advisor stops reporting `extension_in_public`.

Supabase's extension list no longer offers `pg_stat_monitor`, which is a second reason to drop it rather than keep it.

